The observer is one of more photons interacting with the object.  The
fact that the photons detected the object means they hit it.  That
impact changed the direction the object is moving.  That's why the
uncertainty principle exists: The photons that observe also trigger
change.  The only way to know what state something *was* in is to
put it into some other changed.

The reason a particle can't observe itself is it takes something
else triggering its state for an observation to happen.

This all boils down to if someone is watching you plany Nethack,
it's their breath on your neck that really changes your game play.

